            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "- **Perseverance just hit a big driving milestone:** NASA reports the rover has now driven the equivalent of a **full marathon on Mars (26.2 miles / 42.195 km)**. An image from the Mars Reconnaissance Orbiter’s HiRISE camera (taken June 13, 2026) shows the rover as a tiny speck and its track marks across the terrain near a region nicknamed **“Arbot,”** west of Jezero Crater【5:0†source】.\n\n- **New “skywatching” images from the rover:** In early August 2026, NASA highlighted Perseverance imaging **Earth as a bright dot** in the Martian sky as it **passed behind Mars’ moon Phobos** (an occultation), captured as a sequence/composite from Mastcam-Z【5:1†source】【5:3†source】.\n\n- **Autonomy milestone earlier in 2026:** NASA/JPL also announced Perseverance completed the **first AI-planned drives on another world**, where a vision-capable generative AI (vision-language model approach) generated waypoints/routes that the rover then executed (tests ran Dec. 8 and 10, 2025; announced Jan. 30, 2026)【5:4†source】.\n\nIf you tell me whether you want “latest” as *the single most recent NASA update* or *the most notable developments over the last few months*, I can summarize accordingly.",
